 "prompt_sha256": "243160380cdff27ad171171a7f6317d521fcaf508fa2b975c2b2db941e0125e5",
 "answer": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, thereby ensuring that OpenAI is never contacted, you can follow these steps based on the provided context:\n\n1. **Set Up Local LLM with Ollama:**\n   - Utilize Ollama as your local LLM. This choice is suitable for scenarios where you prefer to keep data local, work offline, or manage costs predictably.\n\n2. **Configure Hugging Face Embeddings Locally:**\n   - Use `HuggingFaceEmbedding` to run any Sentence Transformers model locally. This ensures embeddings are generated without contacting external APIs.\n\n3. **Global Configuration with `Settings`:**\n   - Modify the global `Settings` object to specify the local models. This involves setting both the LLM and the embedding model within `Settings`.\n\nHere is a sample configuration in Python:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\nfrom llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\n# Set Ollama as the local LLM in the global settings\nSettings.llm = Ollama(model_name=\"your-ollama-model-name\")\n\n# Set Hugging Face Embedding as the local embedding model in the global settings\nSettings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding(model_name=\"your-sentence-transformers-model-name\")\n\n# Example usage with VectorStoreIndex\nfrom llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\n\n# Create a reader to read documents\nreader = SimpleDirectoryReader(\"path/to/your/documents\")\n\n# Create a VectorStoreIndex using the documents\nindex = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(reader)\n```\n\n### Additional Notes:\n\n- **Ensure Dependencies are Installed:** Make sure you have installed the necessary packages such as `llama-index-ollama` for Ollama and `llama-index-embeddings-huggingface` for Hugging Face embeddings.\n\n- **Model Names:** Replace `\"your-ollama-model-name\"` and `\"your-sentence-transformers-model-name\"` with the actual model names you intend to use.\n\n- **Offline and Local Use:** This setup is ideal for offline usage and ensures all operations are conducted locally without external API calls.\n\n- **Further Resources:** For a step-by-step guide, refer to the local starter tutorial and fully-local RAG cookbook provided in the documentation context.\n\nBy configuring LlamaIndex in this manner, you ensure that all operations are performed using local models, eliminating any interaction with OpenAI or other external services.",
